## Green Christmas Nail Colors

Forest green does more work than almost any other shade on this list. It reads as festive without trying, and it pairs with nearly every outfit already sitting in a holiday wardrobe. Emerald leans brighter and jewel-toned, closer to a statement piece than a background color. Pine green, muted and a touch dusty, works especially well with a matte finish for readers who want green without the shine.

Hunter green sits deepest of the four, almost black in low light, and it holds up through short nails and long alike. Where red can feel like a declaration, green tends to feel like a quieter, more confident choice, one that skips the obvious without skipping the season.

Pair a forest or hunter green with gold hardware or jewelry rather than silver. The warmth carries through the whole look. Explore more shades and pairings in <a href='/blog/christmas-nails/green-christmas-nails' style='color: inherit'>green christmas nails</a>.

