## Blue and Icy Christmas Nail Colors

Blue rarely makes the default Christmas list, and that omission says more about habit than about whether it actually works. Icy blue, pale and nearly frosted, captures a winter mood that red and green can't reach on their own.

Navy carries the most versatility of the group, dark enough to read as formal, warm enough to avoid feeling cold or clinical. Frost white with a blue undertone splits the difference between white and icy blue, best suited to readers who want something quieter than a full color statement. Deeper sapphire, closer to a jewel tone than a pastel, holds its own next to burgundy or emerald without competing.

Blue tends to photograph beautifully under holiday lighting, picking up warmth from string lights in a way flatter colors don't. <a href='/blog/christmas-nails/blue-christmas-nails' style='color: inherit'>Blue christmas nails</a> has more on shade selection.

