## Burgundy and Deep Jewel-Tone Christmas Nail Colors

**Jewel-tone** refers to deep, saturated colors like burgundy, emerald, and sapphire that read as rich rather than bright, the kind of shade that looks expensive without trying to. Burgundy sits at the center of this family, wine-dark and warm, and it may be the single most versatile color on this entire list.

Deep plum leans slightly cooler than burgundy, closer to eggplant, and it suits readers who want jewel-tone depth without the red undertone. True garnet, brighter and more saturated than either, works best for readers already comfortable with bold color. All three finish beautifully in either cream or a soft velvet-style matte, and none of them require glitter or shimmer to feel like an event-ready manicure.

A burgundy or plum manicure carries from an office party through New Year's Eve without needing a repaint, which makes it the closest thing to a one-shade solution on this list.

