## White and Silver Christmas Nail Colors

White and silver rarely get top billing, but they solve a real problem: readers who want something festive without leaning on red, green, or gold at all. Frost white, warmer and softer than a clinical bright white, feels closer to snow than to a blank canvas.

Silver glitter, best used sparingly, adds texture without turning the whole nail into a shimmer statement. A silver chrome finish, applied with a chrome topcoat, pushes the coldest and most formal of the group, best saved for a single event rather than daily December wear. Pearl white, with a soft shimmer built into the polish itself, sits gently between white and silver.

This family works especially well as an accent, one white or silver nail against a stronger color on the rest of the hand, rather than as a full five-finger commitment.

