## Christmas Nail Colors by Occasion

An office party calls for a cream red, champagne gold, or burgundy, colors festive enough to register but restrained enough to stay appropriate in a professional room. Loud glitter and full chrome are easiest to save for later in the season.

Family dinners give more room. Emerald, forest green, and a brighter cherry red all work, since the setting rewards warmth over polish. New Year's Eve is the one night to reach for chrome gold, silver glitter, or icy blue, colors built for a room with better lighting and a later hour. A formal party lands somewhere between the two, where deep jewel tones like plum or sapphire carry the most weight without overreaching.

One shade, most often burgundy or champagne gold, can genuinely carry a reader through all four without a single repaint.

